=== DESIGN ===

Goal: bridge codec atomics -> legacy 5 cross-cutting effects without
coupling normalize.Pipeline to FSM / sessions / alerts. Pattern locked
in 0000 Decision #1: AtomicsObserver injected via variadic constructor.

normalize package surface (post-extension):
  New(histRepo, r, log, observers ...AtomicsObserver) *Pipeline
  Pipeline.Process(ctx, payload, vehicleIntID) error
  type AtomicsObserver interface {
      OnPayloadProcessed(ctx, vehicleID int64, atomics []codec.Atomic)
  }

Lifecycle inside processAtomics:
  1. sortAtomicsSettingUnitFirst(atomics)
  2. for each i in atomics: ctx-check -> processOne(ctx, &atomics[i], vehicleIntID)
     - Setting*Unit short-circuit: Value untouched (proto enum preserved)
     - toSI success: atomics[i].Value mutated in place to SI value, then routed
     - toSI failure: Value left as-is, atomic NOT routed
  3. for each observer in registration order:
     - notifyObserver wraps the call in defer/recover so an observer panic
       is logged + counted but does NOT fail Process
  4. return nil

processOne signature change: now takes *codec.Atomic so the in-place
mutation in step 2 is observable to step 3. The reflective
TestSinglePipelineInvariant only inspects EXPORTED methods, so a private
signature change is invisible to the gate.

Observer execution ordering (locked by Decision #5):
  observers run sequentially in registration order. Production wiring
  registers exactly one observer (SideEffectsObserver). Test wiring may
  register more.

SideEffectsObserver call order inside OnPayloadProcessed (per Decision
#10 (e) + (f) and the prompt's Step 4):
  atomics -> signals (map[string]any) using SIValue per atomic
  vin = vinResolver.VINByID(ctx, vehicleID); on error -> SKIP sessions+alerts only
       (live store / history / FSM / SSE do not need vin and proceed)
  1. live.UpdateAll(ctx, vehicleID, signals)         L1 store
  2. history.Append(vehicleID, signals)              durable history
  3. fsm.ProcessSignals(ctx, vehicleID, signals)     FSM (may read live)
  4. sessions.ProcessSignals(ctx, vehicleID, vin, signals, signals)
     alerts.Evaluate(ctx, vehicleID, vin, signals, signals)
     (the accumulator parameter is the SAME per-payload map per Decision
     #8; the legacy cross-batch accumulator is NOT preserved in the
     bridge — a follow-up prompt may add a tracker if observed
     regressions surface)
  5. broadcastSSE(map[string]any{...}) LAST so the wire view reflects
     all upstream side-effects

Escape hatch evaluation (variadic source-compat):
  Existing live callers of New: 4 in normalize_test.go (TestPipelineHappyPath,
  TestSettingUnitProcessedFirstInSamePayload, plus two more added in this
  prompt's pipeline_test.go + observer_test.go). All compile unchanged
  because variadic observers are an additive parameter. NO call sites
  exceed the 5-site escape-hatch threshold; NewWithObservers shim NOT
  required. New stays a single constructor with a variadic tail.

=== IMPLEMENTATION ===

Files written/modified (4 files in internal/tesla/normalize/, 2 in internal/tesla_pipeline/):

  internal/tesla/normalize/observer.go (NEW, 73 lines)
    - type AtomicsObserver interface { OnPayloadProcessed(ctx, vehicleID, atomics) }
    - Doc comment locks: invocation EXACTLY ONCE per successful payload
      AFTER the route loop; NOT called on codec.Decode failure; observers
      MUST NOT mutate the slice (no defensive copy by Pipeline);
      sequential registration-order execution; panic recovery wraps
      observer invocation; no error return -- observer-internal failures
      are the implementation's own concern.

  internal/tesla/normalize/pipeline.go (MODIFIED)
    - Pipeline gains observers []AtomicsObserver field with godoc
      explaining the architectural seam (ADR-004 #11) and the
      defensive-copy rationale.
    - New(...) extended to variadic observers ...AtomicsObserver tail;
      defensive copy of the variadic slice happens at construction so a
      caller mutating its own backing slice cannot reorder observer
      registration.
    - processAtomics: index-based loop so processOne can mutate
      atomics[i].Value in place after a successful toSI conversion;
      observer fan-out runs at the bottom of the function, after the
      route loop drains; ctx-cancellation between atomics still applies.
    - processOne: receiver argument switched from value codec.Atomic to
      *codec.Atomic so the SI substitution is observable to the
      observer fan-out. Setting*Unit short-circuit and toSI-failure
      paths leave Value unchanged (the codec-original is what
      observers see for those cases).
    - notifyObserver: new helper that wraps a single observer call in
      defer/recover and logs at WARN on panic; subsequent observers
      still run.

